goal_sweep_r2_rollnet_s100":{"t":"2026-11-17 10:21:31","label":"r2 search 100 sims, rollouts buy with the net","note":"","policy":"runs/r2/net_357.npy","n":1000,"score":0.6935,"ci":[0.6642,0.7213],"big_money":0.8425,"smithy_bm":0.7675,"witch_bm":0.655,"sims":100,"lam":0.5,"cpuct":1.5,"ptemp":1.0,"peps":0.0,"rollout_net":1,"secs":790},"goal_sweep_r2_t3c3":{"t":"2026-11-17 10:08:07","label":"r2 search, prior temp 3, cpuct 3","note":"","policy":"runs/r2/net_357.npy","n":1000,"score":0.698,"ci":[0.6688,0.7257],"big_money":0.8725,"smithy_bm":0.7725,"witch_bm":0.6775,"sims":400,"lam":0.5,"cpuct":3.0,"ptemp":3.0,"peps":0.0,"rollout_net":0,"secs":183}},"timeline":{"warm":[],"r1":[],"r2":[],"r3":[],"r4":[]},"decisions":[{"t":"2026-11-17 12:16:43","kind":"decision","title":"Run r4: leaf = value head only (lam = 1), the AlphaZero setting","text":"From r3's net 20, value target = the search's root value (vq = 1), 1 epoch per iteration. With the honest value head, value-only leaves scored 69.7% vs 70.2% for the half-rollout mix, so they are now viable, and they are the only setting in which the judge itself can improve through self-play. Also ~30% faster per simulation. Stop rule: no goal check above ~71% within ~30 iterations.","rejected":"net-buy rollouts (15x slower); more of r3"},{"t":"2026-11-17 10:45:18","kind":"decision","title":"Run r3: value target = the search's root value, fresh value head, 1 epoch","text":"From net 357 with the value head retrained on Q (runs/study/net_357_vq.npy). Each iteration's value target is the search's root value Q instead of the game result (vq = 1), and the buffer is passed once per iteration instead of twice (5 passes per sample instead of 10). Policy target, self-play mix, 400 simulations and lam 0.5 stay as in r2. Measured before starting: the new head's held-out error 0.70 vs 1.24; search with it 70.3% (lam 0.5) and 69.7% (lam 1) vs 70.2% / 68.1% with the old head. The test is whether training with an honest value lifts the plateau. Stop rule: no goal check above ~71% within ~40 iterations.","rejected":"continuing r2 unchanged (flat for 250 iterations); net-buy rollouts (15x slower, +2 points at equal simulations, no better than 400 GA-rollout simulations); softer priors (no gain, 25% uniform 48%)"},{"t":"2026-11-17 09:32:53","kind":"decision","title":"Leaf value: half net, half GA rollout (lam = 0.5)","text":"Measured on the warm-start net vs the GA base, 600 games each: net-only leaves scored 51% / 53% / 48% at 100 / 400 / 1,600 simulations, rollout-only 51% / 54% / 56%, the half-half mix 52% / 58% / 60%. The value net alone is too weak (MSE 0.6) and more search chases its errors; the rollout is unbiased but noisy; the mix wins.","rejected":"lam = 1 (AlphaZero's net-only leaves); lam = 0 (pure rollouts, 30% slower and weaker)"},{"t":"2026-11-17 09:32:53","kind":"decision","title":"Policy target: the search's chosen buy (expert iteration), no root noise","text":"AlphaZero's visit-share target collapsed the net in one iteration (r1: net alone 51.7% \u2192 24.3%): with near-equal buys the shares are the prior plus Dirichlet noise. Completed-Q (Gumbel) barely moves off a sharp prior. The one-hot of the most-visited buy made the net rise (r2). Exploration comes from sampling buys by visits in the first 6 turns and from games against the GA and the bots.","rejected":"visit shares (target 0); completed Q (target 1, c_scale 0.1)"},{"t":"2026-11-17 09:32:53","kind":"decision","title":"Self-play mix: 50% search vs search, 30% vs the GA base, 20% vs the three bots","text":"From iteration 1 to 5 of r2 the score vs the GA base rose (59.8% \u2192 63.0%) while the score vs Big Money / Smithy-BM / Witch-BM fell (78.9% \u2192 76.0%): specialising against one opponent. 20% of games against the bots from iteration 7 held them at ~78%.","rejected":"self-play only against itself; only against the GA"},{"t":"2026-11-17 09:32:53","kind":"decision","title":"Site moved to version 2 of the project-site template","text":"Overview / Log / Training / How it sees / The model (with generated figures of the real net) / Play / Speed / Study / Lessons / Podcast, a status strip on every page. The old one-page Log is now the Log tab; charts and the goal table are on Training.","rejected":""}],"reports":[],"strip":{"alive":false,"run":"r4","stage":null,"goal_text":"65.0%","stages_text":"0 of ? stages passed","best_text":"70.2%","verified_text":"69.8%","verified_sub":"r2 iteration 130 + search, n=1000"}}